          "headersSize": 1048,
          "postData": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "params": [],
            "text": "{\"answer\":\"1. AI: Friend or Foe?\\n\\nAs AI developes it's becoming more and more commonplace in everyday life. Most people have been experimenting with artificial intelligence, many even in multiple different ways. Even companies, big and small, are integrating AI into their products and services. But what does this mean for the average person? Should you be concerned or excited?\\n\\nOne on hand, AI can be used as a writing assistant to enhance a human writer by correcting spelling mistakes and providing feedback during the writing process. AI can also be used for quick prototyping and repetitive responses without using a plain template. Most of the time AI can provide a good enough answer and it's undeniably quicker than doing research by yourself. There definitely are tasks, usually repetitive and small ones, that benefit from and should be done with AI. Human time is valuable, AI doesn't have a limited lifespan.\\n\\nOn the other hand when misused, usually by trusting AI too much or overusing it, you can face more issues than help. AI still definitely hallucinates and makes up information, sometimes even critical things. You should also be wary of how much information you give up to the bots, do you know who is taking a look at the information or is the AI being trained off of your business secrets?\\n\\nIn general AI can be very helpful and lighten up your average day by doing repetitive tasks and short even meaningless tasks that you need done. You should still be wary to not leak your whole personal life and give control over to a chatbot just because it once wrote a nice essay.\"}"
          }
        },
